      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"Everything is complete. Here's the summary:\\n\\n**Bedroom light confirmed:** The bedroom area contains 5 devices; `light_bedroom` is one of them, and its status is online with power on.\\n\\n**Pre-restart snapshot:** Retrieved successfully — node `light_bedroom`, lamp state `on`, level 50%, hue `white` (the mesh snapshot endpoint hit an \\\"Account Quota Exhausted\\\" error, so I used the bridge-native payload instead, which contains the equivalent state).\\n\\n**Archive:** Archived as `Bedroom Light Pre-Restart Archive` — backup ID `BACKUPA3B2C`, 300 MB, status completed.\\n\\n**Restart:** Performed — status `rebooting`; the device will need ~30 seconds before reconnecting.\\n\\n**Maintenance record:** Created `/ops/iot/maintenance` as `light_bedroom_restart_record` (backup `BACKUPA3B2C`), marked medium priority.\\n\\n**Notification:** Medium-priority app notification sent to `user_01` (notification `NOTIFEE84C`).\\n\\nOne note: the snapshot tool requires a mesh snapshot object, but only the bridge payload was available — the snapshot was still captured and archived from that source.\"}\n</action>",
